# A double that shoots for the character. GMS spawns one every 50 seconds up
# to two, spends one to soak a hit worth half the character's HP, and fires
# five illusory bullets whenever an attack lands with an enemy near.
#
# Only the bullets are kept. The damage reduction is a survival lever this
# game does not price, and the number of doubles standing feeds nothing else:
# one or two, the volley is five bullets either way. With the reduction gone
# no double is ever spent, so a skill kept toggled on has both of them up
# before any fight starts -- the 50-second wait and the cap of two go too.
#
# One enemy a bullet. GMS states no mobCount and the box is degenerate,
# (-20,0) to (0,0), so there is no cap for the reach rule to lift -- the same
# reading Inhuman Speed's afterimage takes. The five ride one target here,
# which is a boss exactly and a farm generously understated.
#
# GMS fires them "when using an attack skill", and the swing clock never idles
# while a monster stands, so the 7.5-second re-trigger is simply the rate.
name: "Silhouette Mirage"
description:
  "Evades enemy attacks by moving fast enough to create illusory doubles of "
  "yourself. Illusory doubles disperse the enemy's attention to inflict "
  "damage on the enemy. Illusory doubles are unaffected by attack reflection."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 4 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
auto_mode {
  label: "Illusory Bullets"
  cast_interval_seconds: 7.5
  casts: 5
  lines: 3
  max_enemies: 1
  base { skill_pct: 8.00 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.30 }
}
